# undertown: what lies under the town the company begins in, a step from its door (the owner, 1 November 2026: "we shouldn't have to explore to start an adventuring loop").
// A Kyr template (see src/world/kyr-template.ts). {t} is the town's id, {town} its name; "{{t}_merchant}" is
// written "{s2_merchant}", the merchant's name when it is read. The base and below are always written; of each other
// group one option is drawn for the town. An option of the store, the yard or the pit is a trouble: its name is the
// {pack} and {pair} are how many of the small and middling foes a trouble sets (three and two for one, five and three for
// a company); {brood} is how many of the first foes each trouble sets: two for a company of more than one, one for a company of
// one, as a player begins (a lone first-level mage had died to the corn-store's two great rats three times in four).
// id of the foe it sets there ({t}_u_<option>) and of the job of being rid of it ({t}_u_<option>_job), and its ">>"
// lines are what is said of it on the notice on the green. The notice read is a lead in the Notes, not an aim; a job's
// aim comes of asking the one who gives it (HP-01: the notice had made each job a held aim at once). Add an option
// to add a trouble; nothing in the engine needs to change. An option may be another cause of the same trouble rather
// than another creature: the store's apprentice and runaway are the people its job turns out to be about, not foes
// (the variety study's experiment, mission-22/variety-study/experiment.md). A country of the strategic atlas may fix a group's option (its `fix` in
// data/imbar/atlas.json): Iscoed's first town keeps the rats, so the first-hour route it is measured by holds.
--- base
  // Each fight under the town is worth three times its plain worth, so that a company that clears all of it (some
  // thousand) comes to the stair below the vault at the second level, not the first (the builder's descent of 8
  // November: a lone warrior cleared the town's ten fights at level one, and died at the first of the deep site).
  Relation {t}_u_paid(entity). Relation {t}_u_done(entity). Relation {t}_u_given(entity).
  // Which way down the old ways were first said to go on by: the room the job that said so ended in (see below).
  Relation {t}_u_onward_by(entity).
  // Whether what lives in a room under the town has come at the company already: once, when the company has stood
  // there a while (lingered: searching, lighting, waiting), not as it passes through. Until then it is nowhere, out of
  // sight in the runs, the roof or the dark (a walk through the empty room had stopped at it: main's browser specs).
  Relation {t}_u_came(entity).
  // A job half paid for (done, its cause not yet seen to) is paid only the rest when it is finished (REV-21: the
  // half and then the whole had both been paid).
  Relation {t}_u_halved(entity).
  // A job paid is no longer a lead: its knowing is let go, and it is told among what is done (the Book had listed
  // finished jobs under "Leads: heard, not yet seen": M19-121).
  Place {t}_u_store "the old corn-store" is room within {t} at 0, 1 indoors.
  // Each way down is locked or barred by whoever is troubled by what is under it, and given by them with the job: the
  // troubles had been done without a word to anyone, and paid for after (the owner, 3 November).
  Kind corn_store_key "the corn-store key" like cell_key described "A heavy iron key on a loop of string, with the corn-store's mark burned into its wooden tag.".
  Kind crypt_key "the crypt key" like cell_key described "A long black key, worn smooth, for the stone door into the catacombs under the churchyard.".
  Kind quarry_key "the key to the quarry gate" like cell_key described "A small brass padlock key, for the gate the inn put across the old quarry's adit.".
  Passage {t}_u_store_door "the corn-store door" is door between {t}_green and {t}_u_store.
  // Each locked way is a lock on it: whoever the job is given to holds its key and goes through as if it were open,
  // and anyone with lockwork can pick it instead (Mission 19, a calling's own way in: a thief need not ask).
  Thing {t}_u_store_lock "the corn-store padlock" on {t}_u_store_door {
    // Locked, the padlock is said when the door is tried or the padlock looked at, not as part of the green.
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The corn-store padlock hangs open on its hasp.".
    Change pick "Pick the corn-store padlock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change wrench "Wrench the padlock's hasp out of the old door" from locked to torn needing brawn.
    // Torn, it can be set back by one who can mend, and is forgiven (M21's FF-06: what the job leaves is the next thing).
    Change mend "Set the hasp back in the corn-store door with new bolts" from torn to open needing mending.
    State torn "The hasp hangs out of the corn-store door by one bolt, the oak split round it.".
  }
  // Torn out, it is noticed by whoever owns the store, once, when the company is next before them: a cold player tore
  // the hasp out without asking for the key, and was paid for the rats as if nothing had been done (Mission 20, D).
  Relation {t}_u_hasp_noted(entity).
  // What the merchant does is seen first (M21's FF-05): out at the door, turning the torn hasp over, before any word of
  // it to the company.
  Relation {t}_u_hasp_found(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_hasp_looked when state({t}_u_store_lock, torn) and at(party, {t}_green) and been(party, {t}_u_store) and not {t}_u_hasp_found({t}_u_store_lock) and not {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock)
    says "{{t}_merchant} is out at the corn-store door, turning the torn hasp over. A look round, and back inside." {
    Assert {t}_u_hasp_found({t}_u_store_lock).
  }
  Rule {t}_u_hasp_seen when state({t}_u_store_lock, torn) and {t}_u_hasp_found({t}_u_store_lock) and together({t}_merchant, party) and not {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock) says "{{t}_merchant} does not look up. 'Somebody tore the hasp out of my corn-store door. I had a key for whoever asked.' A look at your hands, then. 'I'll know them by the splinters.'" { Assert {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock). }
  Observe {t}_u_store_lock_shut near {t}_u_store_lock of {t}_u_store_lock when state({t}_u_store_lock, locked) "A padlock the size of a fist hangs on the corn-store door, its hasp bolted through the old oak.".
  Place {t}_u_yard "the churchyard" is room within {t} at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Passage {t}_u_yard_gate "the lych-gate" is gate between {t}_green and {t}_u_yard.
  Place {t}_u_pit "the old quarry pit" is room within {t} at 2, 2 outdoors.
  Passage {t}_u_pit_path "the path down into the old quarry" is path between {t}_green and {t}_u_pit taking 5 minutes.
  // The quarry pit, a place worth returning to (M21's RI-01; the owner, 14 November: knowing more of the world gives
  // more ways to inhabit it). What each company finds here is its own: a ranger reads the fox-runs, a scholar the old
  // mark, and the mark known, the ivy can be pulled off it; a search turns over the spoil, and an hour on the faces
  // finds the quarrymen's ledge. Found, each stays found; by night the vixen is out. Nothing here comes again.
  Entity {t}_u_pit_foxes: fact "Foxes use the old quarry pit at {town}. Their runs go in under the ivy at the foot of its east face. They come and go at dusk.".
  Entity {t}_u_pit_mark: fact "A wheel with no wing is cut low on the north face of the old quarry pit at {town}. It is older than the quarrying: the Road's mark, without its wing.".
  Entity {t}_u_pit_ledge: fact "Halfway up the west face of the old quarry pit at {town}, the quarrymen left a ledge. A niche is cut in its back.".
  Observe {t}_u_pit_runs at {t}_u_pit as sign noticed by woodcraft when not knows(party, {t}_u_pit_foxes) "Runs worn to bare earth go in under the ivy at the foot of the east face. The smell of fox is on them." teaches {t}_u_pit_foxes.
  Observe {t}_u_pit_wheel at {t}_u_pit as sign noticed by lore when not knows(party, {t}_u_pit_mark) "Low on the north face, where the ivy has pulled away, is a mark no quarryman cut. It is a wheel with no wing, its strokes worn soft." teaches {t}_u_pit_mark.
  Person {t}_u_vixen "a vixen" at {t}_u_pit {
    Role "a vixen, thin from her cubs, who keeps the quarry's ivy". Species fox. Pronouns she. Peaceable. Seen when hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5.
  }
  Observe {t}_u_pit_dusk at {t}_u_pit when knows(party, {t}_u_pit_foxes) and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5) "A vixen comes out of the ivy where the runs go in. She sits, and watches you as if you were the one out of place.".
  Thing {t}_u_pit_ivy "the ivy on the north face" at {t}_u_pit {
    State hanging "".
    State pulled "The ivy hangs torn back from the north face, and the wheel with no wing is bare. Under it is cut the word ROAD, smaller and later.".
    Change pull "Pull the ivy back off the wheel on the north face" from hanging to pulled after learning {t}_u_pit_mark.
  }
  Initially Assert answers({t}_u_pit, rummaging).
  Discovery {t}_u_pit_spoil "A carter's luck-stone lay under the spoil at the foot of the west face. It is a flint the size of a fist, worn through with a hole for the string." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_pit "You turn the spoil over, a stone at a time. Under the last of the broken face, a flint with a hole worn through it comes up into your hand. It is somebody's luck, dropped and never found.".
  }
  Relation {t}_u_pit_worked(group).
  Action {t}_u_pit_work(actor: group, site: place) "Work along the faces of the pit, ledge by ledge" {
    Description "An hour on the old faces, climbing where they let you. You look for what the quarrymen left, and what has come since. Once; what it does not find is not there.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_pit) and not benighted(actor) and not {t}_u_pit_worked(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert {t}_u_pit_worked(actor). Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_pit_ledge). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
    Result "Halfway up the west face, a ledge runs along under the ivy. It was the quarrymen's, with a niche cut in its back for their dinners. In it, a purse rotted to a rag, and two coins green with age.".
  }
  Place {t}_u_cellar "the corn-store cellar" is room within {t} at 0, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_trap "the trapdoor" is stair between {t}_u_store and {t}_u_cellar.
  // The way on from the cellar, and its names, are each store trouble's own (the rats' runs, a crawl a man has swept).
  Passage {t}_u_nest_shelf "a shelf above the water" is passage between {t}_u_nest and {t}_u_drain.
  Place {t}_u_crypt "the crypt" is room within {t} at 1, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_crypt_stair "the stone stair under the churchyard" is stair between {t}_u_yard and {t}_u_crypt.
  Thing {t}_u_crypt_lock "the lock of the stone door" on {t}_u_crypt_stair {
    // Locked, said when the door is tried or the lock looked at, as the corn-store's padlock is: told in the room,
    // it said the crypt's door was locked to a company come through it with the key (round 9, Q 74).
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The stone door into the ground stands unlocked.".
    Change pick "Pick the old lock of the stone door" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    // And forced, as any door may be by one strong enough (the owner's evidence session, 7 November: a warrior of
    // twenty strength stood at this door with nothing to do but go and ask for the key).
    Change force "Set your shoulder to the stone door until the old lock gives" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Place {t}_u_ossuary "the ossuary" is room within {t} at 1, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_bone_arch "an arch stacked round with skulls" is arch between {t}_u_crypt and {t}_u_ossuary.
  Place {t}_u_adit "the quarry adit" is room within {t} at 2, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_adit_mouth "the gated adit" is passage between {t}_u_pit and {t}_u_adit.
  Thing {t}_u_adit_lock "the padlock on the adit gate" on {t}_u_adit_mouth {
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The adit gate's padlock hangs open on its chain.".
    Change pick "Pick the brass padlock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change force "Wrench the adit gate's padlock off its staple" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Place {t}_u_gallery "the cut gallery" is room within {t} at 2, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_gallery_way "the old cutting" is passage between {t}_u_adit and {t}_u_gallery.
  // Behind the gallery, where the boy saw the big one: the spiders' mother and her eggs.
  Place {t}_u_brood "the brood-chamber" is room within {t} at 3, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_brood_way "a crack at the back of the gallery, hung with web" is crawl between {t}_u_gallery and {t}_u_brood.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_cellar). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_warren). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_crypt).
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_ossuary). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_adit). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_gallery).
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_nest).
  // The corn-store, locked behind the company, is somewhere to rest between the brood and the nest.
  Initially Assert restful({t}_u_store).
  // What each room under the town is, said on coming down into it (the cellar had said nothing at all: a play of a1's
  // rats on 3 November).
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_scene at {t}_u_crypt as fixture when true "A vaulted crypt under the churchyard, its shelves of coffins pushed askew. The dust on the floor is scuffed through in a dozen places by feet that dragged.".
  Observe {t}_u_ossuary_scene at {t}_u_ossuary as fixture when true "Bones are stacked to the roof in patient courses, with skulls in rows along the top like a frieze. There are gaps in the courses where some have lately been taken down.".
  Observe {t}_u_adit_scene at {t}_u_adit as fixture when true "The old quarry's adit runs straight into the hill, its walls bitten by picks. Grey threads of web cross it at the height of a face.".
  Observe {t}_u_gallery_scene at {t}_u_gallery as fixture when true "A gallery cut square out of the rock, wider than it is high, where the stone was taken out in blocks. The roof is thick with web, and the web is thick with husks.".
--- store apprentice 1
  // Taken by the trapdoor (the variety study, mission-22/variety-study/report.md §5.1 and §8): the merchant's
  // apprentice lets a buyer's men up the drain by night, and the merchant blames rats. From the green it is the same
  // trouble; below, the floor is swept and nothing gnaws. Found first: the swept path (by anyone), the greased bolt
  // (by one who knows locks), the sacks the innkeeper sees on the landing at dawn. The crux is a night's watch and
  // then a word: the lad marched up to the merchant, or talked round and kept. Left too long, he runs.
  // The options of the store are drawn in the order they are written, the plainest last: the rats keep the most weight.
  Observe {t}_u_store_scene at {t}_u_store as fixture when true "Sacks are stacked to the rafters at the front, and there are fewer at the back than there should be. A trapdoor is in the floor. The boards round it are swept clean, though nothing else here is.".
  Place {t}_u_warren "the crawl behind the cellar wall" is room within {t} at 0, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_runs "a hole in the cellar wall" is crawl between {t}_u_cellar and {t}_u_warren.
  Place {t}_u_nest "the shelf over the drain" is room within {t} at 0, 6 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_nest_way "a crawl going down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_nest.
  Observe {t}_u_cellar_scene at {t}_u_cellar as fixture when true "A low brick cellar under the corn-store, damp to the touch. Spilled grain lies over the floor, and the stair is worn pale.".
  Observe {t}_u_warren_scene at {t}_u_warren as fixture when true "A crawlway of earth and old brick runs behind the cellar wall. It is wide enough for a man bent double, and its floor is trodden hard.".
  Observe {t}_u_nest_scene at {t}_u_nest as fixture when true "A dry shelf above the drain water. A rope is tied off to an iron ring in the wall. Grain is spilled at its foot, as from a sack let down.".
  Person {t}_u_apprentice "the apprentice" at {merchantat} {
    Role "the merchant's apprentice, a thin lad floured to the elbows, who keeps the corn-store's tally". Ancestry human. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
  }
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_job: fact "Find what is taking the grain from the corn-store at {town}. Rats, {{t}_merchant} says.".
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_swept: fact "Nothing gnaws under the corn-store at {town}. A path is swept through the cellar's grain to a hole in the wall. Its sweeper comes when the town is asleep.".
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_bolt: fact "The bolt on the corn-store's trapdoor is newly greased. Whoever takes the grain comes and goes by it often.".
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_landing: fact "Twice this week there were sacks on the landing at {town} at dawn. They went into a boat with a ring painted on its bow.".
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_seen: fact "{{t}_merchant}'s apprentice lets men up into the corn-store cellar by night, and they carry the grain away down the drain.".
  Entity {t}_u_apprentice_buyer: fact "The corn-store's grain went down the drain to a boat with a ring painted on its bow, a shilling a sack.".
  Relation {t}_u_apprentice_caught(entity). Relation {t}_u_apprentice_exposed(entity).
  Relation {t}_u_apprentice_kept(entity). Relation {t}_u_apprentice_fled(entity).
  Measure {t}_u_store_given_at(group). Measure {t}_u_thanked_at(group).
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_job_ask with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the rats in the corn-store" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "'Rats,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'A sack a night, near enough, and never a hole gnawed in one of them. Clever rats.' A key comes off a nail behind the counter. At the shelves the apprentice stops what he is doing, and starts again. 'There's a trapdoor in the floor. Find where they get in and stop it. Ten coin, and a lantern besides.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job). Give corn_store_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_store_lock). Set {t}_u_store_given_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_rats with {t}_u_apprentice "Ask the apprentice about the rats" when knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "'Rats,' says the apprentice, to the shelf. 'Big ones. I'd not go down there, me. Not at night.'".
  }
  Observe {t}_u_apprentice_path at {t}_u_cellar as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) "There are no droppings in the spilled grain, and no gnawing on the stair. A broom has swept a path through it to a hole in the far wall." teaches {t}_u_apprentice_swept.
  Observe {t}_u_apprentice_greased at {t}_u_store as sign noticed by lockwork when not knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_bolt) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) "The trapdoor's bolt is greased, and the grease is new. Rats do not grease bolts." teaches {t}_u_apprentice_bolt.
  Observe {t}_u_apprentice_by_day at {t}_u_cellar when knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) and not dark() and not {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) "Whoever sweeps the path comes when the town is asleep: the grain on it is fresh-spilled since last night.".
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_dawn with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the corn-store's rats" when knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_landing) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} snorts. 'Rats? I'm up before light. Twice this week there were sacks on the landing at dawn, going into a boat with a ring painted on its bow. Rats don't row.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_landing). }
  }
  // The crux: a night's watch in the cellar, for whoever has seen that it is no rat.
  Action {t}_u_apprentice_watched(actor: group, site: place) "Wait in the dark of the cellar through the night, and watch the hole in the wall" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_cellar) and dark() and (knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) or knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_bolt) or knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_landing)) and not {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_seen). Retract at({t}_u_apprentice, {merchantat}). Assert at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar). Retract unlit({t}_u_cellar). }
    Result "Late, a light comes through the hole in the far wall. Two men with empty sacks come after it. Behind them, holding the lantern up, is the apprentice of {{t}_merchant}. You step out. The men are back through the hole and away down the drain before the lantern stops swinging. The lad stands where he is, with the light, and does not run.".
  }
  // Then a word, and what the house comes to by it: the lad marched up, or talked round and kept.
  Action {t}_u_apprentice_marched(actor: group, site: place) "Take the apprentice up to {{t}_merchant} by the collar" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_cellar) and at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert {t}_u_apprentice_exposed({t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job). Retract at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar). Assert unlit({t}_u_cellar). }
    Result "{{t}_merchant} comes down in a nightshirt with a candle, and hears it all. The lad is out of the door before the candle is burned down an inch, with what he stood up in. 'Clever rats,' says {{t}_merchant}, to nobody.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_apprentice_talked(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the apprentice it ends tonight, and that {{t}_merchant} need not hear who" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_cellar) and at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert {t}_u_apprentice_kept({t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_buyer). Retract at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar). Assert at({t}_u_apprentice, {merchantat}). Assert unlit({t}_u_cellar). }
    Result "He sits down on the stair. It was a man off a boat with a ring painted on its bow, he says. A shilling a sack, and his mother's rent. He will brick up the hole himself before morning. He goes up the stair ahead of you, and does not look back.".
    Otherwise "'You'll tell him anyway,' he says, and will not look at you.".
  }
  // Left two days and a night unwatched, the lad runs, and takes the seed-corn with him: said wherever the company is.
  Rule {t}_u_apprentice_ran when {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_store_given_at({t}_merchant) + 180
    says "Word goes round {town}: the apprentice of {{t}_merchant} is gone in the night, and the last of the seed-corn with him." {
    Assert {t}_u_apprentice_fled({t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job). Retract at({t}_u_apprentice, {merchantat}).
  }
  Rule {t}_u_apprentice_onward when ({t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job) or ({t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). Assert {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_warren). }
  Milestone {t}_u_apprentice_found "found out what was taking the corn-store's grain" worth 120 when {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job).
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_paid with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} for the ten coin for the corn-store" when {t}_u_apprentice_exposed({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "Ten coin are counted out hard, one at a time. A lantern and two flasks of oil are set beside them. 'I'd sooner it had been rats,' says {{t}_merchant}.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job). Assert grateful({t}_merchant, actor). Set {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_quiet with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the grain will stop going, and not who took it" when {t}_u_apprentice_kept({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "'Not rats, then.' {{t}_merchant} gives the lad at the shelves a long look, and lets it go. Six coin are counted out, and a lantern set beside them. 'Six, for a thing I'm not to know.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Give lantern to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_late with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} what was taking the grain" when {t}_u_apprentice_fled({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job) and (knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) or knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_bolt) or knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_landing)) once {
    Says "'The lad,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'Gone in the night, and you knew it was no rat.' Four coin come across the counter, and no lantern. 'For knowing.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_apprentice_job). }
  }
  // What the house came to, read after by the merchant, the innkeeper and the lad himself (the study's consequence
  // by approach): the lad marched up is gone, and the merchant does the tally; kept, he is a friend who knows the drain.
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_favour with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} how the corn-store is keeping" when grateful({t}_merchant, actor) and {t}_u_apprentice_exposed({t}_u_apprentice_job) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) + 72 once {
    Says "'Dry and quiet,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'I keep the tally myself now.' A candle and a flask of oil come across the counter. 'No charge. You'll be going down again, I don't doubt.'".
    On discuss { Give candle to actor. Give lamp_oil to actor. }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_drain with {t}_u_apprentice "Ask the apprentice about the old drain" when {t}_u_apprentice_kept({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_drain_warm) once {
    Says "The lad looks round for {{t}_merchant} first. 'The men came up it every night. There's a long thing down there, all legs, that lies up by the bakehouse flue where the stone is warm. Keep to the cold side and it won't stir. They always did.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_drain_warm). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_told with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} what is said of the corn-store" when {t}_u_apprentice_exposed({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "'They're saying {{t}_merchant} turned the lad out in a nightshirt,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'And the boat with the ring on its bow has not been in since.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_hushed with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} what is said of the corn-store" when {t}_u_apprentice_kept({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} looks at you. 'The rats just stopped, they say. And the boat with the ring on its bow has not been in since.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_u_apprentice_gone_told with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the apprentice who ran" when {t}_u_apprentice_fled({t}_u_apprentice_job) once {
    Says "'Went off in the boat with the ring on its bow,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'The seed-corn under a sail.' '{{t}_merchant} will be buying seed at the spring price.'".
  }
  Objective {t}_u_apprentice_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) and not knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_bolt) and not knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_landing) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) toward {t}_u_cellar by {t}_u_store "Find what is taking the grain from {{t}_u_cellar}, under {{t}_u_store} at {town}.".
  Objective {t}_u_apprentice_job_watch when (knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_swept) or knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_bolt) or knows(party, {t}_u_apprentice_landing)) and not {t}_u_apprentice_caught({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) toward {t}_u_cellar by {t}_u_store "No rat takes the grain from under {{t}_u_store}. Wait in {{t}_u_cellar} after dark, and see what comes.".
  Objective {t}_u_apprentice_job_word when at({t}_u_apprentice, {t}_u_cellar) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) toward {t}_u_apprentice "The apprentice of {{t}_merchant} stands caught with the lantern in {{t}_u_cellar}. Take him up to {{t}_merchant}, or talk to him.".
  Objective {t}_u_apprentice_job_owed when {t}_u_given({t}_u_apprentice_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_apprentice_job) and not {t}_u_apprentice_fled({t}_u_apprentice_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} the grain will stop going. Ten coin are owed for it, or six for keeping a secret.".
>> 'GRAIN going from the old corn-store, a sack a night. Rats, says {{t}_merchant}. Ten coin, and a lantern. Ask for the key at {{merchantat}}.'
--- store runaway 1
  // Something at the grain that is no rat (the variety study's §8, under its §9 rule that a cause must move the crux
  // into another family than the rats'): a girl run from the mill lives in the crawl behind the cellar wall, on the
  // merchant's grain. Found first: sacks slit as a knife slits, a child's bare prints in the spilled grain, the bread
  // on the step, and, asked, the priest's word of a girl gone from the mill. The crux is a coaxing, not a fight (bread
  // held out, or words), and then where she is sent: to the shrine, or to the merchant. The merchant says the clock:
  // two days, and then poison under the grain; laid, she is gone down the drain.
  Observe {t}_u_store_scene at {t}_u_store as fixture when true "Sacks are stacked to the rafters. Low at the back, three are slit along the seam, neatly, as a knife slits. A trapdoor is in the floor, with a crust of bread on its edge.".
  Place {t}_u_warren "the crawl behind the cellar wall" is room within {t} at 0, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_runs "a hole in the cellar wall" is crawl between {t}_u_cellar and {t}_u_warren.
  Place {t}_u_nest "the shelf over the drain" is room within {t} at 0, 6 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_nest_way "a crawl going down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_nest.
  Observe {t}_u_cellar_scene at {t}_u_cellar as fixture when true "A low brick cellar under the corn-store, damp to the touch. Spilled grain is trodden into the floor, and there are no droppings in it.".
  Observe {t}_u_warren_scene at {t}_u_warren as fixture when true "A crawlway of earth and old brick runs behind the cellar wall. At its end, sacking is heaped into a bed, with a rag doll on it and the crusts of a loaf.".
  Observe {t}_u_nest_scene at {t}_u_nest as fixture when true "A dry shelf above the drain water. The ashes of a small fire are here, made more than once. The dust beside it is pressed flat where a small body slept.".
  Person {t}_u_runaway "the hungry girl" at {t}_u_warren {
    Role "a girl of ten or so, all eyes and elbows, run from a hard master to live on the merchant's grain". Ancestry human. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
  }
  Entity {t}_u_runaway_job: fact "Stop the losses from the corn-store's grain at {town}, before {{t}_merchant} lays poison.".
  Entity {t}_u_runaway_prints: fact "A child goes barefoot in the corn-store cellar at {town}. Small prints in its spilled grain go to a hole in the wall.".
  Entity {t}_u_runaway_who: fact "A girl ran from the mill at the ford before the frosts. Her master said she drowned in the race, and nobody looked.".
  Relation {t}_u_runaway_trusts(entity). Relation {t}_u_runaway_sheltered(entity).
  Relation {t}_u_runaway_handed(entity). Relation {t}_u_runaway_lost(entity).
  Measure {t}_u_store_given_at(group). Measure {t}_u_thanked_at(group).
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_job_ask with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about what is at the grain" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'Something's at my grain,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'Sacks slit, a handful gone at a time, the bread off my sill. A fox, or rats too clever for a trap.' A key comes off a nail behind the counter. 'Rid me of it. Ten coin, and a lantern. Two days, mind. Then I lay poison under the grain myself, and there's an end of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job). Give corn_store_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_store_lock). Set {t}_u_store_given_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Observe {t}_u_runaway_tracks at {t}_u_cellar as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_runaway_prints) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) "In the grain by the far wall are a child's bare prints. They go to a hole low in the wall." teaches {t}_u_runaway_prints.
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_asked with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about a child gone missing" when knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_prints) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_who) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'A child?' {{t}_priest} sits down. 'A girl ran from the mill at the ford before the frosts. Her master said she drowned in the race, and nobody looked.' A breath. 'If it is her, send her here. Not back to him.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_who). }
  }
  // Come at, she is down the hole at the back: what will not do is said before it is tried.
  Observe {t}_u_runaway_wary at {t}_u_warren when at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren) and not {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) "The girl backs into the sacking with a stone in her fist. She will be down the hole at the back if you come a step nearer.".
  // The crux: she is coaxed, by bread held out or by words, and no blow does it.
  Action {t}_u_runaway_fed(actor: group, site: place) "Hold out bread to the girl, and wait" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren) and quantity(actor, rations) >= 1 and not {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job).
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, rations) by 1. Assert {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job). }
    Result "You sit down on the earth with the bread on your open hand, and wait. It is a long time. Then she comes, a step at a time, and takes it. She eats it where she stands. When it is gone she sits down, out of reach, and looks at you.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_runaway_coaxed(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the girl you are not from the mill, and mean her no harm" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren) and not {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job). }
    Result "You say it low, and say it again. The stone goes down. 'Not the mill,' she says. It is the first thing she has said to anyone in a long while.".
    Otherwise "She is down the hole at the back before you have finished, and up again when you have gone quiet. Not yet.".
  }
  // Then where she is sent, and what it makes of the merchant and the priest.
  Action {t}_u_runaway_sent(actor: group, site: place) "Send the girl to {{t}_priest} at the shrine, with your word that she is to be kept" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren) and {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert {t}_u_runaway_sheltered({t}_u_runaway_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren). Assert at({t}_u_runaway, {priestat}). }
    Result "She knows the shrine. She takes the doll and goes up the stair ahead of you. She does not run.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_runaway_given_up(actor: group, site: place) "Take the girl up to {{t}_merchant}, for what she has eaten" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren) and {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert {t}_u_runaway_handed({t}_u_runaway_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren). }
    Result "She comes, because she said she would. {{t}_merchant} looks at her a long time, and sends to the mill at the ford. Her master comes for her before dark.".
  }
  // Two days, as the merchant said, and the poison is laid: said wherever the company is, and she is gone.
  Rule {t}_u_runaway_poison when {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_store_given_at({t}_merchant) + 288
    says "Word comes round {town}: {{t}_merchant} has laid poison under the grain in the corn-store cellar, as promised. By morning the sacks are no longer slit." {
    Assert {t}_u_runaway_lost({t}_u_runaway_job). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract at({t}_u_runaway, {t}_u_warren).
  }
  Rule {t}_u_runaway_onward when ({t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job) or ({t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). Assert {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_warren). }
  Milestone {t}_u_runaway_found "found who was at the corn-store's grain, and won her trust" worth 120 when {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job).
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_paid with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} what has been at the grain" when {t}_u_runaway_sheltered({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'A child. On my corn, all winter.' {{t}_merchant} is quiet a while. Ten coin are counted out, and a lantern and two flasks of oil set beside them. 'Tell the priest there's a sack for her at harvest. And not a word of it to the mill.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_job). Assert grateful({t}_merchant, actor). Set {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_bounty with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} for the ten coin for the corn-store" when {t}_u_runaway_handed({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'Back where she belongs,' says {{t}_merchant}, and counts out ten coin. A lantern and two flasks of oil go on the counter beside them.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_unpaid with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the corn-store" when {t}_u_runaway_lost({t}_u_runaway_job) and {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'The poison saw to it,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'I'll not pay for what poison did.'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_job). }
  }
  // What came of her, read after by the merchant, the priest and the girl herself (consequence by approach): kept at
  // the shrine she tells what she saw below; sent back, the priest says so.
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_favour with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} how the corn-store is keeping" when grateful({t}_merchant, actor) and {t}_u_runaway_sheltered({t}_u_runaway_job) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) + 72 once {
    Says "'Dry and quiet,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'The priest's girl sweeps it out for a loaf.' A candle and a flask of oil come across the counter. 'No charge. You'll be going down again, I don't doubt.'".
    On discuss { Give candle to actor. Give lamp_oil to actor. }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_below with {t}_u_runaway "Ask the girl what she saw down below" when {t}_u_runaway_sheltered({t}_u_runaway_job) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_letters) once {
    Says "'There's letters,' she says, 'on the big stone where the drain goes into the old place. Round in a ring. Three are rubbed deep, like somebody's thumb did it.' She shows you with her own thumb, on the table.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_letters). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_kept with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about the girl from the corn-store" when {t}_u_runaway_sheltered({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "'She sleeps, and she eats,' says {{t}_priest}. 'She has asked twice whether you will come back.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_returned with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about the girl from the corn-store" when {t}_u_runaway_handed({t}_u_runaway_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} does not look up. 'Back at the mill. You did what you were paid for.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_u_runaway_gone with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about the girl from the corn-store" when {t}_u_runaway_lost({t}_u_runaway_job) and knows(actor, {t}_u_runaway_prints) once {
    Says "'Gone down the drain when the poison went down, they say,' says {{t}_priest}. 'A carter saw a girl on the road at first light, alone.'".
  }
  Objective {t}_u_runaway_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job) and not knows(party, {t}_u_runaway_prints) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) toward {t}_u_cellar by {t}_u_store "Find what is at the grain in {{t}_u_cellar}, under {{t}_u_store} at {town}. In two days {{t}_merchant} lays poison.".
  Objective {t}_u_runaway_job_found when knows(party, {t}_u_runaway_prints) and not {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) toward {t}_u_runaway by {t}_u_cellar "A child's bare prints go through the grain. Find who sleeps behind the wall of {{t}_u_cellar}, and come quietly.".
  Objective {t}_u_runaway_job_send when {t}_u_runaway_trusts({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) toward {t}_u_runaway "The girl in {{t}_u_warren} will go where you send her: to {{t}_priest} at the shrine, or up to {{t}_merchant}.".
  Objective {t}_u_runaway_job_owed when {t}_u_given({t}_u_runaway_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_runaway_lost({t}_u_runaway_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_runaway_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} what has been at the grain.".
>> 'Something at the grain in the old corn-store, nights, and the bread off the sill. Ten coin, and a lantern. Ask {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} for the key.'
--- store rats 12
  // The rats: the corn-store is locked and its key is the merchant's, given with the job. A brood in the runs behind
  // the cellar wall, and below them, down their own run into the old drain, the nest and the old buck rat that keeps
  // it: a job of two fights, or of ratsbane and fire for a company that would rather not (Mission 19: the owner found
  // two rats and "it is done" too short to be worth it). The drain below the runs is the undertown's road (see
  // the section below).
  Observe {t}_u_store_scene at {t}_u_store as fixture when true "Sacks are stacked to the rafters, and the place smells of mice. A sack of grain weighs down a trapdoor in the floor, and every wall is gnawed through at its foot.".
  Place {t}_u_warren "the rat-runs" is room within {t} at 0, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_runs "a hole gnawed through the cellar wall" is crawl between {t}_u_cellar and {t}_u_warren.
  Place {t}_u_nest "the nest" is room within {t} at 0, 6 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_nest_way "the rats' run down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_nest.
  Observe {t}_u_cellar_scene at {t}_u_cellar as fixture when true "A low brick cellar under the corn-store, damp to the touch. Spilled grain is trodden black on the floor, among the droppings of something bigger than mice.".
  Observe {t}_u_warren_scene at {t}_u_warren as fixture when true "A crawlway of earth and old brick runs behind the cellar wall, gnawed wider than any rat should need. It is littered with husks and bones, and stinks of a nest.".
  Person {t}_u_rats "the rats under the corn-store" at {t}_u_warren {
    Role "rats, fat and bold, that have eaten their way into the corn-store from below". Species rat.{runts} Numbers {pack}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_warren.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_rats) to 60.
  Person {t}_u_buck "the old buck rat" at {t}_u_nest {
    Role "a rat the size of a dog, grey at the muzzle, with a torn ear and the run of the drain". Species great_rat. Variant elder. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_nest.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_buck) to 120.
  Entity {t}_u_rats_job: fact "Clear the rats out of the corn-store cellar, under the old corn-store at {town}.".
  Entity {t}_u_rats_source: fact "The rats come up into the cellar by a run of their own from their nest below, over the old drain.".
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_ask with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the rats in the corn-store" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "'They've got into the old corn-store from underneath,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'Rats, {nestof}, and bold with it. I've lost a third of the grain.' A key comes off a nail behind the counter. 'There's a trapdoor in the floor. Kill them, and find where they're getting in, or they'll be back by harvest. Ten coin, and I'll see you right for a lantern besides.'{ratsbane}".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job). Give corn_store_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_store_lock). }
  }
  Observe {t}_u_rats_run_seen at {t}_u_warren as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_rats_source) "The rats have worn a path in the dirt along the back wall of the runs. It goes down through the old brickwork, toward the smell of the drain." teaches {t}_u_rats_source.
  Observe {t}_u_nest_scene at {t}_u_nest as fixture when true "A dry shelf above the drain water, heaped with chewed sacking, straw and grain-husks over bones. The stink is enough to make the eyes run.".
  // Nothing done to the nest from far off: the buck rat is too old for bait, but not for fire.
  Action {t}_u_nest_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb into the nest" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, {t}_u_warren) or at(actor, {t}_u_drain)) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_buck).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_buck. }
    Result "The flask bursts on the shelf and the straw goes up at once. Something big comes out of it screaming and goes into the water, and does not come up again.".
  }
  // A magician's way with the rats themselves: a sleep laid over the run, and the rats done for where they lie
  // (Mission 19's Priority Three), for one who would not be bitten. Cast by one who can cast Sleep now, through the one
  // invocation route (the casting-fiction invariant, CF-02/CF-03: the caster's slot, each rat's save; what resists
  // or wakes comes at the company), and no one else.
  Action {t}_u_rats_slept(actor: group, caster: member, site: place) "Have {caster} cast Sleep over the rats in the run" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and able({t}_u_rats) and memberOf(caster, actor) and awake(caster) and canCast(caster, sleep).
    Time 1 minutes.
    Resolve invoke(sleep, caster, {t}_u_rats).
    On success { Assert {t}_u_rats_lulled({t}_u_rats_job). Assert assails({t}_u_rats, actor). }
    Result "The words go out over the run like a breath of cold air. The rats slow and stagger and lie down where they were.".
  }
  // Asleep is not dead (CF-02): the sleepers are done for by a deliberate act, and a band only asleep is not cleared.
  Action {t}_u_rats_done_for(actor: group, site: place) "Do for the sleeping rats where they lie" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and at({t}_u_rats, {t}_u_warren) and not able({t}_u_rats) and not dead({t}_u_rats).
    Resolve combat({t}_u_rats).
    Result "It is quick after that, and not pleasant. None of them wakes for it.".
  }
  Relation {t}_u_rats_lulled(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_rats_cleared when (dead({t}_u_rats) or (not able({t}_u_rats) and not {t}_u_rats_lulled({t}_u_rats_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job). }
  Relation {t}_u_nest_cleared(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_nest_ended when not able({t}_u_buck) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) { Assert {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job). }
  // Fewer, stranger things below (the first hour's beats, 15–35 minutes): the old buck rat keeps what it has dragged in,
  // and sits on it rather than run.
  Observe {t}_u_buck_hoard near {t}_u_buck as sign when able({t}_u_buck) "The old buck rat sits on the heap with a ring round one forefoot. It does not run from your light: it watches what you carry.".
  Discovery {t}_u_nest_hoard "Under the nest's sacking, what the rats dragged in over the years." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_nest "Under the chewed sacking something catches the light.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_nest_ring "a cord of grave rings" is grave_rings at {t}_u_nest hidden until {t}_u_nest_hoard.
  // A way through that needs no fight for the brood in the runs (a lone mage or thief had no way through the first
  // jobs): ratsbane from the chandler's, laid where the rats come up into the cellar, does its work by morning.
  Relation {t}_u_baited(group). Measure {t}_u_baited_at(group).
  Action {t}_u_rats_baited(actor: group, site: place) "Lay ratsbane where the rats come up into the cellar" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_cellar) and holding(actor, ratsbane) and able({t}_u_rats) and not {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats).
    Time 1.
    On success { Spend ratsbane from actor. Assert {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats). Set {t}_u_baited_at({t}_u_rats) to watch(clock). }
    Result "You lay the ratsbane in twists along the foot of the wall where the droppings are thickest. Something scrabbles behind the brick, and goes quiet. By morning, it will have done its work.".
  }
  Rule {t}_u_rats_poisoned when {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats) and able({t}_u_rats) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_baited_at({t}_u_rats) + 36 { Slay {t}_u_rats. }
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_u_cellar, {t}_u_rats by {t}_u_store "Clear the rats out of {{t}_u_cellar}, under {{t}_u_store} at {town}, and find where they get in.".
  // The cellar's rats dead and how they came up not yet found, the job's second half is still asked: it had dropped
  // out of the aim unsaid, and the cold player was never told where they got in (cold play 5, CL-35).
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_way when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and not knows(party, {t}_u_rats_source) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_u_warren by {t}_u_cellar "The rats in {{t}_u_cellar} are dead. Find where they got in: there will be more where they came from.".
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_run when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_rats_source) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_u_nest, {t}_u_buck by {t}_u_warren "Clear the nest down the rats' run from {{t}_u_warren} under {{t}_u_store}. Deal with the old buck rat that keeps it, or they will be back.".
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_paid with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats under the corn-store are dead, nest and all" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_merchant} hears about the nest and the old buck rat with a face that says the grain is the least of it. Ten coin are counted out, and a lantern and two flasks of oil set on the counter beside them. 'That drain goes under half the town,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'If you're going back down it, go with a light that won't blow out.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). Assert grateful({t}_merchant, actor). Set {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_rest with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats' nest in the drain is cleared" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_merchant} hears about the nest and the old buck rat, and counts out the other four coin. A lantern and two flasks of oil go on the counter beside them. 'That drain goes under half the town,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'If you're going back down it, go with a light that won't blow out.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). Assert grateful({t}_merchant, actor). Set {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_half with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats under the corn-store are dead" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "'Dead,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'And the rest of them coming up the same way they came, I don't doubt.' Six coin are counted out. 'Find where they come from and clear it. Then you'll have the other four, and the lantern.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job). }
  }
  // Owed only to a company that took the job, and "the rest" only once half was paid: one that had killed the rats
  // unasked had been told of the rest of a pay it had never been offered (round 6, I 144, J 38).
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_owed when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} that the rats and their nest are dealt with. The rest of the pay is yours, and a lantern.".
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_owed_whole when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} that the rats and their nest are dealt with. Ten coin are yours, and a lantern.".
>> 'RATS in the old corn-store, a nest of them. Ten coin, and a lantern. Ask {{t}_merchant} at {{merchantat}} for the key.'
  Rule {t}_u_rats_onward when ({t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) or ({t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). Assert {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_warren). }
  // By force or by craft, the job is paid, and the merchant remembers which (M21's FF-04). A door torn open is docked
  // from the pay, unless it was mended first; rats laid by ratsbane are smelt on the one who laid it.
  Relation {t}_u_docked(entity). Relation {t}_u_mended(entity). Relation {t}_u_bait_told(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_door_docked when {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) and state({t}_u_store_lock, torn) and together({t}_merchant, party) and not {t}_u_docked({t}_u_store_lock)
    says "{{t}_merchant} takes two of the coins back off the counter. 'For my door.'" {
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 2. Assert {t}_u_docked({t}_u_store_lock).
  }
  Rule {t}_u_bait_smelt when {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats) and together({t}_merchant, party) and not {t}_u_bait_told({t}_u_rats)
    says "{{t}_merchant} sniffs at your sleeve. 'Ratsbane. Cheaper than a sword, and no blood on the sacks.'" {
    Assert {t}_u_bait_told({t}_u_rats).
  }
  // A favour remembered (M21's paragon pin, in FF-06): the rats seen to, the merchant is grateful, and greets the
  // company as a friend; come back a day on, and there is a friend's price on what lights the way down.
  Measure {t}_u_thanked_at(group).
  Topic {t}_u_favour with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} how the corn-store is keeping" when grateful({t}_merchant, actor) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_thanked_at({t}_merchant) + 72 once {
    Says "'Dry and quiet,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'The grain is going out by the cartload.' A candle and a flask of oil come across the counter. 'No charge. You'll be going down again, I don't doubt.'".
    On discuss { Give candle to actor. Give lamp_oil to actor. }
  }
  // The torn door is the next thing asked, in the merchant's own words (FF-06): set back, it is forgiven.
  Objective {t}_u_door_owed when {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock) and state({t}_u_store_lock, torn) and not {t}_u_docked({t}_u_store_lock) toward {t}_u_store "{{t}_merchant} will know you by the splinters. Set the corn-store's hasp back, or be docked for the door.".
  Rule {t}_u_door_mended when {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock) and state({t}_u_store_lock, open) and together({t}_merchant, party) and not {t}_u_mended({t}_u_store_lock)
    says "{{t}_merchant} has been to look at the corn-store door. 'New bolts,' {{t}_merchant} says, and nods once." {
    Assert {t}_u_mended({t}_u_store_lock).
  }
  // What the rats found first under the sacks: a strongbox someone hid down here, its corner gnawed. Not the
  // merchant's, who says whose it was when asked: a room with something in it that sends the company back up (the owner, 19 November: rooms with nothing in them, and quests that do not circle back).
  Discovery {t}_u_cellar_box "Under the gnawed sacks, a little iron strongbox, its corner chewed through." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_cellar "Under the gnawed sacks in the corner, the edge of an iron box.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_cellar_purse "an old corn-factor's purse" is steel_coin at {t}_u_cellar hidden until {t}_u_cellar_box.
  Topic {t}_u_cellar_box_asked with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the strongbox under the cellar sacks" when knows(actor, {t}_u_cellar_box) once {
    Says "{{t}_merchant} turns the empty box over and laughs once. 'Not mine. The old corn-factor kept the store before me. He went off owing half the town. Keep what was in it. If he comes asking, you never saw it.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
--- yard dead
  // The dead: they have not come up of themselves. Someone has been opening graves by night and raising what was in
  // them with a black candle in the ossuary; the churchyard, the crypt and the lodger at the inn say so to whoever
  // looks, and the dead lie down again when the candle is out, by a fight or by words (the owner, 3 November: the
  // dead had come with no hint of why, and nothing to find out).
  Observe {t}_u_yard_scene at {t}_u_yard as fixture when true "Old stones lean in the grass. In the corner by the wall, a low stone door goes into the ground. Its iron ring is bright where someone has pulled at it lately.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_robbed: fact "Someone has been opening graves in the churchyard by night, and going down into the catacombs.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_raised: fact "The dead under the churchyard have been raised. A ring of chalk and the ends of black candles are on the crypt floor.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_lodger: fact "A man lodging at the inn goes out after dark. He comes back before light with grave-dirt on his boots.".
  Observe {t}_u_yard_graves at {t}_u_yard as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_robbed) "Three graves by the wall have been dug into and filled again badly. The grass is trodden flat from them to the stone door." teaches {t}_u_dead_robbed.
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_circle at {t}_u_crypt as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_raised) "On the crypt floor is a ring of chalk with marks round it. Inside it, the ends of black candles are burned to the floor." teaches {t}_u_dead_raised.
  Person {t}_u_dead "the hungry dead of the ossuary" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    Role "dead things raised out of the bone-heaps, hungry". Species ghoul. Numbers {brood}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_ossuary.
  }
  Initially Assert tolerates({t}_u_dead, party).
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_dead) to 75.
  Person {t}_u_raiser "the man with the black candle" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    Role "a grave-robber who has read a book he should not have, and is trying what it says". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 2. Temperament defensive. Lair {t}_u_ossuary. Pronouns he.
    Warns "A man in a muddy coat stands up behind a burning black candle, among the bones. 'Go back up,' he says. 'This is not yours.'".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_raiser) to 90.
  // Spoken to, he has something to say of himself, not only dice to be rolled against him (cold play 6, CL-54's 15).
  Topic {t}_u_raiser_who with {t}_u_raiser "Ask the man with the black candle who he is" when able({t}_u_raiser) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) once {
    Says "'A reader,' he says. 'I took a book out of a grave, and it says the dead will answer if they are asked properly.' The flame on the skull does not move. 'I have been asking. They have not said anything I wanted yet.'".
  }
  // His dead stand with him while the candle burns: a fight with him is with them (the man died to one blow, alone,
  // with his dead looking on: Mission 20's fourth round, F 100–101). Pinching the candle out is still the way past.
  Initially Assert beside({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_raiser).
  Thing {t}_u_candle "the black candle" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    State alight "A black candle burns on a skull in the middle of the bone-heaps, with a flame that does not move.".
    State snuffed "The black candle is out, and smells of something worse than tallow.".
    Change pinch "Pinch out the black candle" from alight to snuffed when not at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) or not able({t}_u_raiser) "The man with the black candle stands over it, and the dead are his while it burns.".
  }
  Entity {t}_u_dead_job: fact "Lay the dead in the crypt under the churchyard at {town}.".
  // Not once the job is done: a warrior who forced the crypt door and laid the dead had still been offered the job,
  // and the key, after the pay (the owner, 7 November). So for each job asked of.
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_ask with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about the noises under the churchyard" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} looks at the floor. 'The catacombs. Something has come up out of the bone-heaps, and there have been lights in the churchyard at night that were not mine.' The crypt key is unhooked from a belt. 'I cannot ask anyone to go. If you will, lay them, and find out who is doing it. Fifteen coin, and what the shrine can give besides.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job). Give crypt_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_crypt_lock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_lodger_ask with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} who goes out at night" when knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_robbed) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} wipes the same place on the counter twice. 'There's a man in the back room, been here a fortnight, pays in old coin. Goes out after dark and comes in before light. There's grave-dirt on his boots that I scrub off the step.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger). }
  }
  // The lodger the innkeeper tells of is the man with the black candle, and is found: going down the crypt stair by
  // night, and known for himself in the ossuary (round 9, Q: told of, never found; a night watching the churchyard
  // had said "Nothing comes").
  Observe {t}_u_lodger_goes at {t}_u_yard as sign when dark() and knows(party, {t}_u_dead_lodger) and able({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) "Late, a man in good boots crosses the churchyard with a lantern shuttered to a slit. He goes down the crypt stair without looking back. The innkeeper's lodger keeps his hours.".
  Observe {t}_u_lodger_known at {t}_u_ossuary when knows(party, {t}_u_dead_lodger) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) "There is grave-dirt to the ankles of his good boots: the man who lodges at the inn and pays in old coin.".
  Action {t}_u_raiser_talked(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the man with the black candle the town knows what he has done, and that it ends now" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_raised) and state({t}_u_candle, alight).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "He looks at you a long time over the flame, and then at the dead. Then he wets his fingers and pinches the candle out. He goes past you up the stair without a word, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "'They'll hang me whether I stop or not,' he says, and lifts the candle higher. The dead turn their heads.".
  }
  // A priest's way, and a scholar's (Mission 19: a calling's knowledge makes a different ending): the rite of rest
  // said over the bone-heaps puts the candle out from where it stands; and one who knows the old scripts reads in the
  // chalk ring what the raiser's book left out, and can tell him so.
  Action {t}_u_dead_rested(actor: group, site: place) "Say the rite of rest over the bone-heaps, against the black candle" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "You say the words for the dead that every shrine keeps, slowly, as they are meant to be said. The flame on the black candle leans as if a door had opened somewhere, and goes out. The man in the muddy coat looks at you as if you had struck him. He goes up the stair at a run, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "The words come, but the black candle's flame does not move. The dead turn their heads toward the sound.".
  }
  // A thief's way (journey 2 of Mission 19, 7 November: the same opening played as a cleric and as a thief, the
  // cleric had the rite and a scholar the chalk, and the thief nothing of a thief's own here): round behind the
  // bone-heaps, out of his candle's light, to pinch it out from behind him. Seen, the dead are no longer his to hold.
  Action {t}_u_candle_crept(actor: group, site: place) "Creep round behind the bone-heaps and pinch out the black candle at his back" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    On failure { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
    Result "You go back the way you came and round, along the foot of the bone-heaps where his candle throws no light. You come up behind him. He hears nothing until the flame is a wisp between your fingers. He turns and sees the dead fall, and runs. He is up the stair and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "A skull rolls off the course under your hand and goes down the heap, knocking. He turns with the candle held high, and the dead turn with him.".
  }
  // The book he leaves on the bones, as each ending says, is there to be taken (M19-143: it was told, and Search found
  // nothing): left when he goes, or dropped when he falls.
  // A book, read: taken, it had had no Read row (cold play 6, CL-56).
  Kind raiser_book "a book of the dead" is document teaching {t}_u_dead_read worth 6 weighing 1 described "A small fat book in a scraped calf binding, copied out by several hands over a long time. It holds rites for the dead. In the margins, in a newer hand, is how they might be called back up. Someone has drawn the chalk ring on the last page and got it wrong.".
  Entity {t}_u_book_left: fact "The raiser's book of the dead lies on the bones in the ossuary.".
  Item {t}_u_raiser_book "a book of the dead" is raiser_book at {t}_u_ossuary hidden until {t}_u_book_left.
  Rule {t}_u_book_dropped when ({t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) or not able({t}_u_raiser)) and at(party, {t}_u_ossuary) and not knows(party, {t}_u_book_left) says "His book lies on the bones." teaches {t}_u_book_left { }
  Entity {t}_u_dead_read: fact "The marks round the chalk ring are copied badly, from an old book of the dead: the warding line is left out. The dead are held only while the candle burns, and whoever holds them is not safe from them.".
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_marks at {t}_u_crypt as sign when capable(party, lore) and knows(party, {t}_u_dead_raised) and not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_read) "You know these marks from the old scripts. The warding line is missing from the marks round the chalk ring, the one that keeps the dead off whoever calls them." teaches {t}_u_dead_read.
  Action {t}_u_raiser_read(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the man with the black candle what his book left out of the ring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_read) and state({t}_u_candle, alight).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "You tell him about the warding line. He looks down at the chalk, and you watch him find the place where it should be. His hand shakes when he pinches the candle out. He goes up the stair without looking at the dead, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
  }
  // His while he stands, and only bones once the candle is out: with him gone and it still burning they are no one's,
  // and turn on the living, warning first, so there is a moment to pinch it out.
  Rule {t}_u_dead_masterless when not at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and tolerates({t}_u_dead, party) says "With no one to hold them, the dead turn their heads toward the living." { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_masterless_fallen when not able({t}_u_raiser) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and tolerates({t}_u_dead, party) says "With no one to hold them, the dead turn their heads toward the living." { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_lie when state({t}_u_candle, snuffed) and at({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_dead) says "With the candle out, the dead fold down into the bone-heaps like coats let fall, and are only bones again." { Retract at({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_cleared when not able({t}_u_dead) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job). }
  Rule {t}_u_raiser_ended when not able({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
  // Toward the dead themselves and whoever raised them (its own words: "and find out who raised them"), by the
  // churchyard: the crypt is where the priest said they came up, but they are in the
  // ossuary beyond it, and an aim that pointed at the crypt left a company that had been through the ossuary standing
  // in the crypt led only to search it (the owner's play of 11 November: led to the threshold and abandoned there).
  Objective {t}_u_dead_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) toward {t}_u_dead, {t}_u_raiser by {t}_u_yard "Lay the dead in {{t}_u_crypt} under {{t}_u_yard} at {town}, and find out who raised them.".
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_paid with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the dead under the churchyard are laid, and the man who raised them gone" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} hears it all with eyes shut. At the end come the names of the three in the opened graves, one after another. Then 15 coin. From the shrine's own chest come a charm of ashwood and bronze wire, and two small stoppered bottles. 'The charm was made for those who go among the dead,' {{t}_priest} says. 'The bottles are for after.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 15. Give ashwood_charm to actor. Give 2 minor_healing_potion to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_rest with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the man who raised the dead under the churchyard is gone" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} hears it all with eyes shut. At the end come the names of the three in the opened graves, one after another. Then the rest of the coin. From the shrine's own chest come a charm of ashwood and bronze wire, and two small stoppered bottles. 'The charm was made for those who go among the dead,' {{t}_priest} says. 'The bottles are for after.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Give ashwood_charm to actor. Give 2 minor_healing_potion to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_half with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the dead under the churchyard are laid" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "'Laid,' says {{t}_priest}, 'until whoever raised them comes back with another candle.' Ten coin. 'Find who it is. Then the rest is yours, and more.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Objective {t}_u_dead_job_owed when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) toward {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} at {{priestat}} that the dead are laid, and the man who raised them gone. Fifteen coin are yours, and what the shrine can give.".
>> 'Whoever will go down into the catacombs under the churchyard, where something has come up: fifteen coin, and the shrine's thanks. Ask {{t}_priest} at {{priestat}}.'
  Rule {t}_u_dead_onward when ({t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) or ({t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). Assert {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_ossuary). }
  // The crypt's own, before the ossuary: bats in its vault that the raiser's comings and goings have kept stirred, and
  // that come down at a light (the owner, 19 November: the dungeons "deathly dull … almost no content or combat").
  Person {t}_u_crypt_bats "the bats in the crypt" nowhere {
    Role "bats roosting in the crypt's vault, that wheel down shrieking when a light comes in". Species bat. Numbers {pack}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_crypt.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_crypt_bats) to 30.
  Rule {t}_u_crypt_bats_come when at(party, {t}_u_crypt) and lingered(party) >= 1 and able({t}_u_crypt_bats) and not {t}_u_came({t}_u_crypt_bats) says "The roof of the crypt is moving: bats, and the nearest come down shrieking." { Assert at({t}_u_crypt_bats, {t}_u_crypt). Assert assails({t}_u_crypt_bats, party). Assert {t}_u_came({t}_u_crypt_bats). }
  // Dropped by the coffins: the inn's own brass token, of the kind given to a lodger for the back stair. Whoever comes
  // down here lodges at the inn; the innkeeper says who, asked of it, so the crypt sends the company back up (the owner, 19 November: rooms with nothing in them, and quests that do not circle back).
  Discovery {t}_u_crypt_token "By the coffins, a brass token stamped with the inn's sign: a lodger's, for the back stair." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_crypt "In the dust by the pushed coffins, a small brass token.".
  }
  Topic {t}_u_crypt_token_asked with {t}_innkeeper "Show {{t}_innkeeper} the brass token from the crypt" when knows(actor, {t}_u_crypt_token) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} turns the token over. 'That's my back-stair token. The man in the back room has it. He has been here a fortnight and pays in old coin. He goes out after dark. He comes in before light with grave-dirt on his boots.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger). }
  }
--- pit spiders
  // The spiders: the quarry's gate is the inn's, given with the job; the Hobb boy who went in after his ferret saw the
  // mother at the back and dropped his father's knife; the spiders dead and their egg-sacs burned, the inn pays in what
  // a company going on needs, and the knife given back is the Hobbs' to repay.
  Observe {t}_u_pit_scene at {t}_u_pit as fixture when true "A bowl of grey stone cut out of the hill long ago, ivy over its faces. At the bottom a square adit goes back into the rock behind a barred gate. A board on the gate says KEEP OUT in three hands.".
  // Told at the door (PL-07: two great cave spiders killed a first-level warrior in two fights of three, placements.md):
  // what they leave in the web across the adit, seen by anyone with a light, before the gallery.
  Observe {t}_u_husks at {t}_u_adit when able({t}_u_spiders) "Things hang in the web across the cutting ahead, wrapped grey and sucked dry. A fox, a dog, something the size of a calf. Whatever strung it takes prey that big.".
  Person {t}_u_spiders "{spiders} in the old workings" at {t}_u_gallery {
    Role "{webbed} strung the old workings with web". Species cave_spider. Numbers {brood}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_gallery.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_spiders) to 60.
  Person {t}_u_mother "the spiders' mother" at {t}_u_brood {
    Role "a spider the size of a pony, swollen and slow, crouched over the eggs at the back of the web". Species cave_spider. Variant brood_mother. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament defensive. Lair {t}_u_brood.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_mother) to 120.
  Person {t}_u_hobb "Dannel Hobb" at {innkeeperat} { Role "a boy of ten with a white streak in his hair, kept indoors". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. }
  Entity {t}_u_spiders_job: fact "Burn the spiders out of the quarry adit under the old quarry pit at {town}.".
  Entity {t}_u_spiders_eggs: fact "The spiders' mother has hung her eggs at the back of the old workings. Unless they are burned, the spiders will come again.".
  Kind hobb_knife "a bone-handled knife" like dagger worth 2 weighing 1 described "A working man's knife with a bone handle, H burned into it.".
  // With the key, a remedy for the bite: a cave spider's venom stays in the blood after the fight, and a lone first
  // company bitten once had died of it at full health (the builder's descent of 8 November).
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_ask with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the old quarry" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "'Nobody goes in the old quarry now,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'There's webs across the adit thick as sailcloth. The Hobb boy went in after a ferret and came out white. We put a gate on it.' A small key, put down on the counter. 'Twelve coin from the house to whoever burns them out, and a pot of the salve the firemen use. Talk to the boy first. He saw more than he says.' A stoppered phial follows it, the cork waxed. 'Hobb's mother made that, for the bite. Drink it the moment one has you, not after.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job). Give quarry_key to actor. Give antidote to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_adit_lock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hobb_told with {t}_u_hobb "Ask Dannel Hobb what he saw in the old quarry" when knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) once {
    Says "The boy looks at the door before he answers. 'There's a big one at the back,' he says. 'Bigger than a dog. And bags. Hanging up, white, like puddings. They was moving.' He swallows. 'I dropped Dad's knife. Don't tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_eggs). }
  }
  // A ranger's way (Mission 19): one who reads wild country reads the web at the adit, and knows what the boy saw
  // without asking him.
  Observe {t}_u_adit_web at {t}_u_adit as sign when capable(party, woodcraft) and not knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) "Something big at the back is laying: the web across the cutting is new at the edges and old in the middle. The drag-lines all run back one way." teaches {t}_u_spiders_eggs.
  Discovery {t}_u_knife_found "Under the web at the gallery's mouth, a bone-handled knife with an H burned into the handle." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_gallery "Something under the web at the gallery's mouth catches the light.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_knife "a bone-handled knife" is hobb_knife at {t}_u_gallery hidden until {t}_u_knife_found.
  Thing {t}_u_eggs "the spiders' egg-sacs" at {t}_u_brood {
    State hanging "White sacs the size of loaves hang from the roof in a cluster, and something in them moves.".
    State burnt "Where the egg-sacs hung there is a black stain on the roof and a smell of burnt hair.".
    Change burn "Burn the egg-sacs" from hanging to burnt needing flame when not able({t}_u_mother) "The spiders' mother crouches over them, and will not let you near.".
  }
  // An oil firebomb thrown through the crack does for the mother and the eggs both, for a company that would not go in.
  // A flask thrown, or a spell said, takes moments, not a turn of the clock: taking a turn, it had been cut short by the
  // spiders' patience, and a cold player threw it into a fight that said nothing of it (Mission 20, log E32).
  Action {t}_u_brood_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb through the crack into the brood-chamber" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_gallery) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_mother).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_mother. Retract state({t}_u_eggs, hanging). Assert state({t}_u_eggs, burnt). }
    Result "The flask bursts somewhere behind the web, and the crack fills with light. Something heavy thrashes in there a long while, and then the only sound is the sacs popping in the heat.".
  }
  // A magician's way (Mission 19's Priority Three: a magician's spells should make actual alternatives): fire from the
  // hands, thrown through the crack as the flask is, for no flask.
  Action {t}_u_brood_spelled(actor: group, site: place) "Burn the brood-chamber through the crack with a magician's fire" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_gallery) and able({t}_u_mother) and memberOf(?m, actor) and awake(?m) and (hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) or learned(?m, firebolt) or learned(?m, burning_hands) or learned(?m, scald)).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Slay {t}_u_mother. Retract state({t}_u_eggs, hanging). Assert state({t}_u_eggs, burnt). }
    Result "The words come out cold and the fire comes out hot. It goes through the crack in a sheet, and the web catches like paper. Something heavy thrashes behind it a long while, and then the only sound is the sacs popping in the heat.".
  }
  // A way through for a company that would not stand in the web: an oil firebomb thrown into it from the adit, and the
  // fire runs up it into the gallery. The egg-sacs at the back are still to be seen to.
  Action {t}_u_spiders_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb into the web across the cutting" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_adit) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_spiders).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_spiders. }
    Result "The flask bursts against the web. The fire runs up it into the dark of the cutting, faster than you would have thought. Something screams in a voice like wet wood in a grate. When it has burned out, nothing moves in there.".
  }
  Rule {t}_u_spiders_cleared when not able({t}_u_spiders) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job). }
  // Toward where the spiders are, the gallery past the adit: toward the adit, the gold had led back out of the
  // gallery with the spiders in it, "the way you came" (rounds 10 and 11, R and U).
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) toward {t}_u_gallery by {t}_u_pit "Burn the spiders out of {{t}_u_adit} under {{t}_u_pit} at {town}.".
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_eggs when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and able({t}_u_mother) toward {t}_u_brood "Deal with the spiders' mother in {{t}_u_brood} behind the quarry's gallery, and burn her eggs, or the spiders will come again.".
  // With her dead, what is left is the eggs: "deal with the spiders' mother" had stood under the fight that killed her
  // (round 10, R 100).
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_burn when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and not able({t}_u_mother) toward {t}_u_brood "Burn the spiders' eggs in {{t}_u_brood} behind the quarry's gallery, or the spiders will come again.".
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_paid with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders in the old quarry are dead, and their eggs burned" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} counts out 12 coin, and sets a clay pot and a coil of good rope beside it. 'Fireman's salve, and the rope from the gate,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'We'll not want it now.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Give fireproof_salve to actor. Give rope to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_rest with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders' eggs in the old quarry are burned" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} counts out the other five coin, and sets a clay pot and a coil of good rope beside it. 'Fireman's salve, and the rope from the gate,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'We'll not want it now.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Give fireproof_salve to actor. Give rope to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_half with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders in the old quarry are dead" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "'And the eggs?' says {{t}_innkeeper}, and sees your face. 'Then they'll be back by spring.' Seven coin. 'Burn them and the rest is yours.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 7. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hobb_knife with {t}_u_hobb "Give Dannel Hobb his father's knife back" when holding(actor, hobb_knife) once {
    Says "The boy takes it in both hands. That evening his mother comes to find you, with a bottle wrapped in a cloth. 'From the boy,' she says. 'It's what I had by me.'".
    On discuss { Spend hobb_knife from actor. Give minor_healing_potion to actor. }
  }
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_owed when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) toward {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} at {{innkeeperat}} that the spiders are dead and their eggs burned. Twelve coin are yours, with salve and rope.".
>> 'SPIDERS in the old quarry. Twelve coin from the house. Ask {{t}_innkeeper} at {{innkeeperat}} for the gate key.'
  Rule {t}_u_spiders_onward when ({t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) or ({t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job))) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). Assert {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_gallery). }
  // The old cutting's cracked roof, shored with the quarrymen's timbers or passed under at a risk (the owner, 19
  // November: the dungeons "deathly dull"). Nothing feeds at the foot of the web: fewer, stranger things below.
  Thing {t}_u_cutting_roof "the roof of the old cutting" on {t}_u_gallery_way {
    State loose dangerous "Stones have come down from the roof of the cutting, and more hang cracked above it.".
    State shored "A prop of old timber holds up the cracked roof of the cutting.".
    Hurts with {t}_u_cutting_fall when loose then loose.
    Change shore "Shore up the cracked roof with the quarrymen's old timbers" from loose to shored needing brawn.
  }
  Hazard {t}_u_cutting_fall "Stone falling from the cutting's roof" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (11).".
--- below
  Place {t}_u_drain "the old drain" is room within {t} at 0, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_drain_way "a culvert going down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_drain.
  // A job done under the town is not the end of what is under it (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon is more than one or
  // two rooms; the undertown's three ways meet, and go on down, and nothing had said so). Each trouble, done, says the
  // old ways go on; the undercroft they meet in is the next place to go, its floor the next thing to try, its vault's
  // keeper the next to face; and below him the deep site (see RegionUndertown).
  Entity {t}_u_onward: fact "".
  // Said as the job is paid (the one who paid says the old ways go on), and so followed on from the job as its next
  // part, toward the undercroft the three ways meet in: it had come as the job's first half was done, one aim among
  // the town's with no place it was toward, and the gold had gone up to be paid and off to the next job on the
  // notice, the drain, the undercroft and the vault under it never led to (the first quarter hour's census, 19
  // November; the owner: "a random chain of quests that don't circle back"). By the room that job ended in, whose ways
  // down are then the aim's (AimRoute.onward): toward a place never seen, nothing in the town had been gold.
  Objective {t}_u_onward_sought when {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) and not been(party, {t}_u_undercroft) and {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_warren) toward {t}_u_undercroft by {t}_u_warren "The old ways under {town} go on past the corn-store's cellar. The rat-runs lead into an old drain. Steps go down behind the ossuary's bone-heaps, and a breach opens in the quarry gallery's floor. They meet below, in {{t}_u_undercroft}.".
  Objective {t}_u_onward_sought_yard when {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) and not been(party, {t}_u_undercroft) and {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_ossuary) toward {t}_u_undercroft by {t}_u_ossuary "The old ways under {town} go on past the corn-store's cellar. The rat-runs lead into an old drain. Steps go down behind the ossuary's bone-heaps, and a breach opens in the quarry gallery's floor. They meet below, in {{t}_u_undercroft}.".
  Objective {t}_u_onward_sought_pit when {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) and not been(party, {t}_u_undercroft) and {t}_u_onward_by({t}_u_gallery) toward {t}_u_undercroft by {t}_u_gallery "The old ways under {town} go on past the corn-store's cellar. The rat-runs lead into an old drain. Steps go down behind the ossuary's bone-heaps, and a breach opens in the quarry gallery's floor. They meet below, in {{t}_u_undercroft}.".
  Objective {t}_u_floor_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_flag_seen) and not knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) toward {t}_u_undercroft "Something is under the floor of {{t}_u_undercroft}: one flag cut with letters does not sit level. The same ring may be cut somewhere in the ways down to it.".
  Place {t}_u_undercroft "the undercroft" is room within {t} at 1, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_drain_mouth "the mouth of the drain" is passage between {t}_u_drain and {t}_u_undercroft.
  // Each way down is more than the room its job ends in (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon is more than one or two
  // rooms): behind the bone-heaps a charnel passage where the raiser's first tries were left to stand, and off the
  // gallery the old working face the spiders came up from, a beetles' nest now.
  Place {t}_u_charnel "the charnel passage" is room within {t} at 1, 4 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_charnel_arch "a low arch behind the bone-heaps" is passage between {t}_u_ossuary and {t}_u_charnel.
  Passage {t}_u_ossuary_steps "steps down behind the bone-heaps" is steps between {t}_u_charnel and {t}_u_undercroft.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_charnel).
  Observe {t}_u_charnel_scene at {t}_u_charnel as fixture when true "A long low passage lined with shelves of the older dead, wrapped in cloth gone brown. Some of the shelves are empty, and the cloth on the floor under them is torn.".
  Person {t}_u_shamblers "the dead in the charnel passage" at {t}_u_charnel {
    Role "the raiser's first tries, stood up off the shelves and left where they stood". Species zombie. Numbers {pair}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_charnel.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_shamblers) to 90.
  // And the raiser's first tries go on with what they were last told to do.
  Observe {t}_u_shamblers_folding near {t}_u_shamblers as sign when able({t}_u_shamblers) "The dead in the passage are folding the brown cloth from the empty shelves. They do it slowly, and over again.".

  // The raiser's first tries are his candle's too: with it out they go down where they stand, and the job is not paid
  // over dead still standing in the charnel passage (cold play 3, CL-20; the variety study's §10).
  Rule {t}_u_charnel_lie when state({t}_u_candle, snuffed) and at({t}_u_shamblers, {t}_u_charnel) and able({t}_u_shamblers) says "In the charnel passage behind the bone-heaps, the dead fall down too." { Retract at({t}_u_shamblers, {t}_u_charnel). }
  Discovery {t}_u_charnel_goods "On the last shelf, under a fall of cloth, lies what the old dead were buried with. Nobody has been down to take it." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_charnel "Under the cloth on the last shelf, something hard and cold.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_charnel_plate "a silver grave-plate" is chapel_plate at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Item {t}_u_charnel_torc "an iron torc" is iron_torc at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Item {t}_u_charnel_bracelet "a bronze bracelet" is bronze_bracelet at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Place {t}_u_face "the old working face" is room within {t} at 2, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_face_way "a cut going on past the web" is passage between {t}_u_gallery and {t}_u_face.
  Passage {t}_u_gallery_breach "a breach in the gallery floor" is crawl between {t}_u_face and {t}_u_undercroft.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_face).
  // Nothing lives at the face (BP-07: fewer, more credible dangers): its beetles had no job and no story, a stocked
  // fight between the spiders' gallery and the undercroft. The face is the quarrymen's, and what they left.
  Observe {t}_u_face_scene at {t}_u_face as fixture when true "Where the quarrymen stopped: a face of stone with the pick-marks still on it, and a rotten ladder. In one corner the floor is broken through into somewhere older underneath. Nothing has moved the spoil since they left it.".
  Discovery {t}_u_face_tools "Under the ladder is a quarryman's bag, left when the face was given up. In it are his tools, and his wages, never collected." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_face "A leather bag under the ladder, stiff with age.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_face_crowbar "a quarryman's crowbar" is crowbar at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Item {t}_u_face_purse "a quarryman's wages" is steel_coin at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Item {t}_u_face_garnet "a garnet in the spoil" is garnet at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_drain). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_undercroft).
  // Where the three ways meet, nothing lives: a company can rest there between them (the builder's descent of 8
  // November: nowhere under the town could a company recover, and a lone warrior went into her seventh fight hurt).
  Initially Assert restful({t}_u_undercroft).
  Observe {t}_u_drain_scene at {t}_u_drain as fixture when true "An old drain of fitted stone, tall enough to stoop along, with a black trickle down the middle. The walls are furred with something pale that moves when the light touches it.".
  Observe {t}_u_undercroft_scene at {t}_u_undercroft as fixture when true "A long room of round pillars, older than anything above it. The corn-store, the church and the quarry were all dug down into it from three sides.".
  // The flag is a sign of its own, so the page says it apart and searching is the act it leads with.
  // Seen, the flag is known: the aim of it had come with being in the undercroft, in the dark, before anything could be
  // seen there (cold play 6, CL-56).
  Entity {t}_u_flag_seen: fact "One flag in the undercroft floor is cut with a ring of letters, and does not sit level.".
  Observe {t}_u_undercroft_flag at {t}_u_undercroft as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) "One flag in the middle of the floor is cut with a ring of letters nobody here can read. It does not sit quite level with the rest." teaches {t}_u_flag_seen.
  Person {t}_u_crawler "a great centipede" at {t}_u_drain {
    Role "a centipede as long as a man, living in the old drain". Species great_centipede. Numbers 1. Level 2. Lair {t}_u_drain.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_crawler) to 60.
  // What is known above opens a better way below (M21's FF-02): asked about the old drain, the innkeeper tells where
  // its centipede lies up; known, the company keeps to the cold side, and it does not stir.
  Entity {t}_u_drain_warm: fact "The old drain's centipede lies up by the bakehouse flue, where the stone is warm. It does not stir for one who keeps to the cold side.".
  Topic {t}_u_drain_asked with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the old drain under {town}" when not knows(actor, {t}_u_drain_warm) once {
    Says "'The old drain?' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'There's a long thing down there, all legs. It lies up by the bakehouse flue, where the stone is warm. Keep to the cold side and it won't stir.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_drain_warm). }
  }
  Action {t}_u_drain_cold(actor: group, site: place) "Keep to the cold side of the drain, away from the warm stone" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_drain) and knows(actor, {t}_u_drain_warm) and able({t}_u_crawler) and not tolerates({t}_u_crawler, actor).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates({t}_u_crawler, actor). }
    Result "You keep to the cold wall, single file, the light low. By the warm stone something long shifts its legs, and lets you by.".
  }
  Discovery {t}_u_drain_cache_found "Wedged in the drain where the water would have carried it, a purse someone dropped down a grating long ago." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_drain "Something wedged in the drain, where the water left it.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_drain_purse "a mouldy purse" is steel_coin at {t}_u_drain hidden until {t}_u_drain_cache_found.
  // The culvert down from the runs breathes out the drain's foul air, until the cellar's trapdoor is propped open and
  // the air moves (the owner, 19 November: the dungeons "deathly dull … almost no content or combat").
  Thing {t}_u_culvert_air "the air in the culvert" on {t}_u_drain_way {
    State foul dangerous "The culvert breathes out a stink of old water and rot that catches in the throat.".
    State clear "Air moves down the culvert now, from the cellar above.".
    Hurts with {t}_u_drain_foul when foul then foul.
    Change prop "Prop the trapdoor open above and let the air down the culvert" from foul to clear needing brawn.
  }
  Hazard {t}_u_drain_foul "The foul air of the culvert" means "Deal (1d4) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (11).".
--- vault
  // The lettered flag is a lock with no keyhole (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon has at least one puzzle). Its ring of
  // letters is the makers' own, and the same ring is cut, smaller, in each of the three ways down to it, over the
  // oldest thing there: read in any of them, the letters to press are the three cut deeper than the rest. One who
  // knows old writing reads them off the flag itself. A strong arm can lever it up instead, slowly, and loudly.
  Entity {t}_u_vault_found: fact "The lettered flag in the undercroft floor lifts: under it, a stair going down into the dark.".
  // Said as what is seen where it is found: told "on the undercroft's flag … here too", it had spoken of an undercroft
  // the company had never seen (rounds 10 and 11, R 107, U 135).
  Discovery {t}_u_letters "A ring of letters is cut small over the oldest stone of the old work. Three of them are cut deeper than the rest, worn smooth by thumbs, as if pressed." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_ossuary "Over the oldest niche, behind the bone-heaps, a ring of letters cut small, three of them deeper than the rest.".
    Found by searching {t}_u_brood "Under the webs, on the one dressed stone in the chamber's wall, a ring of letters is cut small. Three of them are worn deep.".
    Found by searching {t}_u_drain "On the keystone where the drain meets the old work, a ring of letters cut small, three of them worn deep.".
  }
  // Pressing the letters, or reading them, wants them seen: in the undercroft's pitch dark they had been offered to be
  // pressed (cold play 6). Levering the flag up is done by feel.
  Action {t}_u_flag_pressed(actor: group, site: place) "Press the three deep-cut letters on the flag, as the ring below has them" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and knows(actor, {t}_u_letters) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found). }
    Result "One, then the next, then the last. Each gives a little under your thumb, with a click somewhere under the floor. The flag sinks a finger's width, and slides aside on its own weight. Under it, a stair goes down into the dark.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_flag_read(actor: group, site: place) "Read the ring of letters on the flag" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and capable(actor, lore) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_letters) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_letters). }
    Result "The letters are the makers' own, and run round the flag twice over. Their pattern is not a word at all but a count. Three of them, read as numbers, are cut deeper than the rest. Pressed in their order, they would be the key.".
    Otherwise "The letters are the makers' own, and you cannot make them out. The same ring may be cut somewhere else, where whoever cut it meant it to be read.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_flag_levered(actor: group, site: place) "Lever the lettered flag up by main force" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found). }
    Result "It takes most of an hour, and the edge of everything you have that will take a strain. The flag comes up grinding, and something in the floor below breaks with a sound like a bell. Under it, a stair goes down into the dark. Below, something has heard you.".
    Otherwise "The flag does not move, and an hour is gone. It was not made to be lifted.".
  }
  Place {t}_u_vault "the sealed vault" is room within {t} at 1, 6 underground 3 down.
  Passage {t}_u_vault_stair "the stair under the lettered flag" is stair between {t}_u_undercroft and {t}_u_vault hidden until {t}_u_vault_found.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_vault).
  Observe {t}_u_vault_scene at {t}_u_vault as fixture when true "A small square vault, dry as an oven, smelling of old spice. A stone chair stands at the far end, and niches in the walls once kept something.".
  // The barrow ghoul (the SRD's, ghoul/barrow), alone, at the bottom of what the town's fights bring a company to the
  // second level for: the deepest room had been the easiest (a first-level warrior won 95 % against Orsino's ghoul
  // here); never in the ossuary's brood, where the SRD ghoul killed what had been won (placements.md, PL-07).
  Person {t}_u_keeper "the keeper of the vault" at {t}_u_vault {
    Role "the last of whoever built the undercroft, long dead and still at its post". Species ghoul. Variant barrow. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_vault.
    Warns "Something stands up from a stone chair at the far end of the vault. It rises slowly, as if it had been waiting a long time.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_keeper) to 300.
  Item {t}_u_vault_rings "a cord of old rings" is grave_rings at {t}_u_vault.
  Item {t}_u_vault_stone "a moonstone the size of a thumb" is moonstone at {t}_u_vault.
  Milestone {t}_u_vault_reached "found the sealed vault under the undercroft" worth 25 when been(party, {t}_u_vault).
  Objective {t}_u_vault_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) and able({t}_u_keeper) toward {t}_u_vault "Something keeps {{t}_u_vault} under the undercroft.".
--- hand sellsword 1
  // Someone on the green who would come along (the owner, 19 November, AT-08: in the very first space, in general,
  // someone recruitable; the first choices, companions or alone). Its own draw (keyed), so no other draw moves.
  Person {t}_u_hand "the sellsword on the green" at {t}_green {
    Role "a sellsword between masters, sitting on the well-kerb with a notched blade across her knees". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns she.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the sellsword what work she is after" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "She looks you over. 'Going down under this town? Then I'll come. Two coin, and a share.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 2. }
  }
--- hand acolyte 1
  Person {t}_u_hand "the runaway acolyte" at {t}_green {
    Role "an acolyte run from a shrine two valleys over, still in his grey habit, counting the coppers in his palm". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the acolyte where he is going" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "He counts the coppers in his palm. 'I know the rites for the dead. Feed me and I'll come.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 0. }
  }
--- hand tinker 1
  Person {t}_u_hand "the tinker's daughter" at {t}_green {
    Role "a tinker's daughter left behind when the cart went on, picking a lock on a strongbox for the fun of it". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the tinker's daughter why she was left behind" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "The lock clicks open under her pick. 'He'll be back at harvest. Till then I go where the locks are. One coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 1. }
  }
// Who is on the green is drawn by how the company's life began, where the life has its own people (the difference
// census's first proposal: the first town's cast had been the same few for every life): a drover's town has a drover's
// lad, a debtor's a bailiff's man owed by the same creditor, an heir to the weir an eel-boy, a salt-raker's a raker
// laid off, a son come home his father's old carter's boy. Each would come along, as the others would.
--- hand drover 3 if fromdrove
  Person {t}_u_hand "the drover's lad" at {t}_green {
    Role "a drover's lad from over the fells, his dog at his heel and no drove to follow". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the drover's lad where his drove went" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "'Sold at the march, and me with nothing to drive,' says the lad. The dog looks up at him. 'I can walk all day. One coin, and the dog comes too.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 1. }
  }
--- hand bailiff 3 if fromdebt
  Person {t}_u_hand "the bailiff's man" at {t}_green {
    Role "a bailiff's man in a good coat gone thin, owed a month's wages by the same merchant you owe". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the bailiff's man what he is waiting for" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "'My wages,' he says. 'Same as you're waiting to pay, I expect.' He stands up. 'Two coin, and I'll help you find it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 2. }
  }
--- hand eelboy 3 if fromweir
  Person {t}_u_hand "the eel-boy" at {t}_green {
    Role "an eel-boy with a trap on his back, who has never seen the sea-gate shut". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the eel-boy what he wants" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "'To see it shut,' says the boy. 'Just once. I'll carry. I'll not eat much.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 0. }
  }
--- hand raker 3 if frompans
  Person {t}_u_hand "the laid-off raker" at {t}_green {
    Role "a salt-raker laid off when the fires went out, salt still in the creases of her hands". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns she.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the raker what she will do now" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "'Whatever pays,' she says. 'Not raking. Two coin, and I'll go where you go.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 2. }
  }
--- hand carter 3 if fromkin
  Person {t}_u_hand "the carter's boy" at {t}_green {
    Role "the boy who used to hold your father's horse, grown now, and still looking down the road". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hand_ask with {t}_u_hand "Ask the carter's boy whether he saw the cart go" when not willing({t}_u_hand, actor) and not travelsWith({t}_u_hand, actor) once {
    Says "'I held the horse while he loaded,' says the boy. 'He said he'd be back by dark.' He looks down the road. 'I'll come and look. For nothing.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing({t}_u_hand, actor). Set hire({t}_u_hand) to 0. }
  }
